        "iid": 4122,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "feat: support setting work item iteration id",
        "description": "## Description\n\nAdd an `--iteration <id>` flag to `glab work-items create` and `glab work-items update`, so you can schedule a work item in an iteration without using the UI or GraphQL.\n\n- The flag takes the numeric iteration ID, which `glab iteration list -F json` shows. It doesn't look up iterations by title, because iterations from automatic cadences have no title.\n- The value goes to `IterationID` on `gitlab.CreateWorkItemOptions` and `gitlab.UpdateWorkItemOptions`. Both already exist in the pinned `client-go` v3.23.0, so no dependency bump is needed.\n- Both commands use `Flags().Changed(\"iteration\")` to tell whether the flag was set, so leaving it out never sends an iteration.\n- `docs/source/work-items/` is regenerated with `make gen-docs`.\n\nRemoving an iteration is out of scope. `client-go` omits a nil `IterationID`, so it can't send the `null` that GraphQL needs to clear the field.\n\n## Related Issues\n\nResolves #8622\n\n## How has this been tested?\n\n- New unit tests in `create_test.go` and `update_test.go`, using the `client-go` mocks through `cmdtest.SetupCmdForTest`:\n  - `TestWorkItems{Create,Update}_Iteration`: `--iteration 123` sends `IterationID` `123`, and leaving the flag out sends no `IterationID`.\n  - `TestWorkItems{Create,Update}_FlagValidation`: a non-numeric `--iteration` value is rejected.\n- `go test ./internal/commands/workitems/...` passes.\n- `golangci-lint run --new-from-rev=origin/main ./internal/commands/workitems/...` (2.14.0, Go 1.27.2) reports 0 issues.\n- `make check-args check-embed` passes.\n\n## Screenshots (if appropriate):",
